  "articleBody": "Ever wonder if you need a permit to finish your garage walls with drywall? It’s a good question, and the answer often depends on where you live and the specifics of your project. In many cities, like those around the Denver metro area, if you’re finishing a framed wall in your garage for the very first time, a permit might be required. This is especially true if your garage is attached to your home or if there's a habitable room above it, due to fire-rating requirements. The local building department wants to ensure that the proper fire-rated drywall (like Type X) is used to maintain safety. Getting a permit helps confirm that your project meets these critical safety and structural codes. Skipping the permit process can lead to headaches down the line, including potential fines, having to redo work, or issues when you sell your home. It’s always best to check with your local municipality before you start. If the thought of navigating permits and code requirements feels overwhelming, don't worry! That's where professional help can really come in handy. We can help make sure your project is compliant from the get-go.",
